<div class="content-block">
    <p>Every audit, every regulatory review, and every customer security questionnaire eventually asks the same underlying question: how do you know your controls actually satisfy your requirements? Security Controls Mapping and Traceability is the discipline that answers that question. It connects what a system must do, what mechanism makes that true, and what framework documents recognize it, all the way through to the proof that it works.</p>

    <p>This room builds the mental model and practical skill of a security engineer who owns that proof. You will learn to map requirements to controls, trace a single control across NIST 800-53, ISO 27001, and CIS Controls, and build the matrix that ties it all together. A hands-on lab lets you build a real controls matrix from scratch.</p>

    <h3>Learning Objectives</h3>
